-- title:
--   Atkin–Lehner automorphism transports moduli places along a q-isogeny
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q'$, and let $N,q$ be nonzero naturals with $q$ prime, $q \nmid N$ and $q' \nmid Nq$. Write $F_{Nq} = \kappa(\,j,\,j_{Nq}\,)$ for `modularFunctionFieldC κ (N * q)`, the intermediate field of the Laurent series field over $\kappa$ generated by the $q$-expansions `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ (N*q)`, and assume the expansions `jqNModC κ N` and `jqNModC κ q` lie in it. Let $\sigma$ be a $\kappa$-algebra automorphism of $F_{Nq}$ which is an Atkin–Lehner level automorphism at $q$, i.e. $\sigma$ interchanges `jqModC κ` with `jqNModC κ q` and interchanges `jqNModC κ (N*q)` with `jqNModC κ N`. Let $E/\kappa$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve, $C$ a cyclic subgroup of its affine point group with $\mathrm{card}\,C = Nq$, and $Q \in C$ of additive order $q$. Then there exist an elliptic Weierstrass curve $E'$ and a homomorphism $\varphi : E(\kappa) \to E'(\kappa)$ of additive groups such that: $\varphi$ lies in `rationalHomSet κ E E'` (it is zero or rationally represented); $\ker \varphi = \langle Q\rangle$; $\varphi$ is surjective; $\varphi$ is universal among rational homomorphisms killing $Q$, in that for every elliptic $V$ and every $\alpha \in$ `rationalHomSet κ E V` with $\alpha Q = 0$ there is $\gamma \in$ `rationalHomSet κ E' V` with $\alpha = \gamma \circ \varphi$; and, for every place $P$ of $F_{Nq}$ over $\kappa$ (a valuation subring containing $\kappa$, proper, and a principal ideal ring) whose valuation subring is the restriction along the inclusion $F_{Nq} \subseteq$ `modularFunctionFieldFullC κ (N*q)` of that of the moduli place `moduliPlace κ (N*q) E C`, the valuation subring of the place $\sigma$-transported from $P$ by `autOnPlaces κ N q σ` is the restriction along the same inclusion of the valuation subring of `moduliPlace κ (N*q) E' ((C ⊔ (q • AddMonoidHom.id _).ker).map φ)`, the moduli place of $E'$ with the image under $\varphi$ of $C + E[q]$.
--
--   This is the moduli-theoretic description of the Atkin–Lehner involution $w_q$ on $X_0(Nq)$, which on enhanced elliptic curves sends $(E,C)$ to $(E/C[q],\,(C+E[q])/C[q])$, here expressed at the level of valuation subrings of places of the level-$Nq$ modular function field restricted from the full-level field. It supplies the Atkin–Lehner half of the two-level transport of moduli places used in [`CerednikDrinfeld.autOnPlaces_eq_of_isAtkinLehnerLevelAut_of_forall_toValuationSubring_eq_comap_moduliPlace`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.autOnPlaces_eq_of_isAtkinLehnerLevelAut_of_forall_toValuationSubring_eq_comap_moduliPlace).
